{
	"version": 5,
	"id": "BTrv7hGxT41Ms4L6t",
	"notes": "A Chaos Sorcerer: a Legionary who has traded some of his body's training for mastery of the warp, most famously the Thousand Sons and the sorcerers of every Legion and warband. Built as the Chaos Space Marine with IQ 14 and Will 16 (the framework figures: IQ +3 over the Legionary and Will 17 from the package, so Will is reduced by one), Psyker (Talent) 3 counting the Mark of Tzeentch's +1, Warp Empowerment 20 (the Alpha level, power cap 210, as the Librarian) and the Mark of Tzeentch in place of Mark of Chaos Undivided. About 1289 points before gear. Powers: Smite 12d(10) burn (162) and Fire Bolt 12d burn (42), each within the Empowerment cap of 210; Warp Empowerment 20 leaves room to add Assail, Haemorrhage or Witch-sight from the same file. A GM may swap the powers for other disciplines in Imperium/Traits/Psykers and the Warp.adq. Equipment: Mark IV heretic plate, force staff, bolt pistol. The Mark's Paranoia and Compulsive Lying are in the template.",
	"traits": [
		{
			"id": "TtxA-_bB9kyVrKioK",
			"name": "Astartes",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Adeptus Astartes: a superhuman created by grafting nineteen engineered organs onto a chosen human recruit and finishing the process with years of training and psycho-indoctrination. This trait is the baseline shared by every Chapter's gene-seed; Chapter lenses below add or remove pieces where the fiction says a specific lineage differs.\n\nDesign: 407 (Attribute Modifiers) + 152 (nineteen organs: 4+14+1+6+5+8+5+1 +11+14+9+9+11+7+21+20+4+1+1) + (-2) (Hypno-Indoctrination) + 10 (Enhanced Move 1/2) + 6 (Extended Lifespan 3) = 573 points. This is the physiology alone, before any skills; see the Battle-Brother, Scout, and Primaris templates for full characters built on top of it.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
			"container_type": "ancestry",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tnkoDiQS1p9PpwCq1",
					"name": "Attribute Modifiers",
					"local_notes": "Design: Increased ST +20 (B14, 10/level, 200) for ST 30 (user's figure), which also raises base HP to 30. Raised from ST 18 when weapon damage was rescaled: at ST 30 a Marine lifts nine times what a baseline human can (Basic Lift 180 lb), matching fiction of Astartes tearing open hatches and lifting men one-handed, and a single bolt that gets through the armour (avg ~40 with its follow-up) leaves him fighting rather than dead. Increased HT +4 (B15, 10/level, 40) for HT 14. Increased Basic Speed +1.00 (B17, 5 points per 0.25, 20) for \"faster reflexes than baseline humans\" without inflating every DX-based skill the way a straight DX buy would. Increased Will +2 (B16, 5/level, 10) for the iron discipline the fiction shows even before the Hypno-Indoctrination package below. Extra Hit Points +4 (B16, 2/level, 8) for HP 34: Astartes survive wounds that would kill several men, beyond what ST alone gives. Extra Fatigue Points +3 (B16, 3/level, 9) for FP 17, matching fiction of Marines fighting for days without rest. Increased DX +5 (B15, 20/level, 100) at the user's direction: Astartes are faster and more precise than any baseline human, so a Battle-Brother reaches DX 16 with his own training. Basic Move +4 (B17, 5/level, 20) at the user's direction: a Marine sprints at around 45 km/h in full plate. 200+100+40+20+20+10+8+9 = 407. Height runs 2.1-2.4 m per the framework; SM stays 0 unarmoured.",
					"tags": [
						"Physical"
					],
					"base_points": 407,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "st",
							"amount": 20
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "dx",
							"amount": 5
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "ht",
							"amount": 4
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "basic_speed",
							"amount": 1
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "basic_move",
							"amount": 4
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "will",
							"amount": 2
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "hp",
							"amount": 4
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "fp",
							"amount": 3
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "tuAoqKzWnhKNhmpcV",
					"name": "Enhanced Move (Ground)",
					"reference": "B52",
					"local_notes": "Top sprinting speed x1.5 (Move 12 sprints at 18 yd/s, about 60 km/h). Combat Move unchanged.\n\nLore: Astartes cover open ground at a pace no human can match, even in full plate: the fiction repeatedly shows Marines running down fleeing enemies and closing on gun lines faster than they can be tracked.\n\nDesign: Enhanced Move (Ground) 1/2 (B52, 20/level, half level 10) at the user's direction that Marines run very fast; stacks with the package's Basic Move +4. Half a level, not a full one, keeps the Custodes (a full level) clearly faster.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Adeptus Astartes"
					],
					"points_per_level": 20,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 0.5
				},
				{
					"id": "tfSF8g2Uobn7qS8KD",
					"name": "Extended Lifespan",
					"reference": "B53",
					"local_notes": "Ages far more slowly; centuries of service are routine. A GM may remove it for a Chapter or campaign that treats Marines as short-lived.",
					"points_per_level": 2,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 3
				},
				{
					"id": "tvu6Dyj97E58PUGWl",
					"name": "Secondary Heart",
					"reference": "B58",
					"local_notes": "+2 to HT rolls made solely to avoid death (Hard to Kill 2).\n\nLore: A backup heart grown alongside the original, wired into the same circulatory system so the body keeps pumping blood even if the primary heart is destroyed or stops. Widely depicted in Black Library fiction as one reason Astartes shrug off wounds that would drop a normal man dead of shock or blood loss.\n\nDesign: Modelled as Hard to Kill 2 (B58): +2 to HT rolls to avoid death only, not a general toughness bonus, since the second heart is a redundancy against cardiac failure specifically. 2 x 2 = 4 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Imperium",
						"Adeptus Astartes"
					],
					"base_points": 4
				},
				{
					"id": "tYXi40P8MFRK0Dpz9",
					"name": "Ossmodula",
					"reference": "B46",
					"local_notes": "DR 3 on torso and vitals only (fused, armoured ribcage). Stacks with worn armour.\n\nLore: Triggers a second, controlled growth spurt: the skeleton is re-knitted around a denser mineral lattice, ribs fuse into an armoured cage, and the whole frame roughly doubles in mass over the following implantation. The fused ribcage is one of the most consistently described Astartes traits: a solid plate of bone over the chest that turns blades and slugs that would reach a normal man's heart.\n\nDesign: The ST/HT/HP payoff of the growth process is bought once in the Astartes Attribute Modifiers, not here. What the organ adds on its own is the fused ribcage: Damage Resistance 3 (B46, 5/level, 15) with the Partial (torso and vitals) limitation, -10%, = 13.5, rounded up to 14. An earlier draft priced this as a 1-point perk with no mechanical effect, which left the most-cited Astartes toughness feature out of play.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Imperium",
						"Adeptus Astartes"
					],
					"base_points": 14,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "dr_bonus",
							"locations": [
								"torso",
								"vitals"
							],
							"amount": 3
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "tRLs0vEMSh_A12acI",
					"name": "Biscopea",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Works alongside the Ossmodula to pack the newly-grown frame with dense, fast-twitch muscle, giving Astartes their characteristic bulk.\n\nDesign: Same reasoning as Ossmodula: the muscle mass is paid for once as part of the racial ST bonus, so this is a 1-point Perk marking the organ's presence rather than a second helping of ST.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Imperium",
						"Adeptus Astartes",
						"Perk"
					],
					"base_points": 1
				},
				{
					"id": "TsxURI9ZOvVa4fHkJ",
					"name": "Haemastamen",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Regulates the chemistry of Astartes blood and produces the genetically-tagged compounds an Apothecary tests for to confirm a Marine's gene-seed lineage and general biochemical stability. Its output is also the substrate Larraman's Organ acts on, and the same tuned blood chemistry is why Astartes so seldom fall to ordinary disease.\n\nDesign: 1-point Perk (B21) for the lineage-marker function, plus Resistant (B81) to Disease: Occasional hazard 10, +8 tier x1/2 = 5 points. A bonus rather than Immunity, because the fiction has Marines fall to warp-spawned and engineered plagues. 6 points total.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Imperium",
						"Adeptus Astartes"
					],
					"container_type": "meta_trait",
					"children": [
						{
							"id": "t6_3HkGNiCmnY-5pc",
							"name": "Haemastamen (Gene-Seed Markers)",
							"local_notes": "Plot-hook marker; an Apothecary can confirm lineage and biochemical stability from the blood.",
							"tags": [
								"Perk"
							],
							"base_points": 1
						},
						{
							"id": "tBrNoZK_kjlxLOKHi",
							"name": "Resistant to Disease",
							"reference": "B81",
							"local_notes": "+8 to HT rolls to resist disease (Occasional hazard, +8 tier).",
							"base_points": 5,
							"round_down": true
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "tMXPEiV9RpObPUTkP",
					"name": "Larraman's Organ",
					"reference": "B79",
					"local_notes": "Wounds scab and scar over within seconds rather than minutes; treat as Rapid Healing for recovery rolls (B424), and the GM should waive ongoing blood-loss effects from an untreated wound after the first turn.\n\nLore: Floods the bloodstream with \"Larraman's cells\" that clot almost instantly on exposure to air, so an open wound scabs over in seconds. This is the single most commonly cited reason Astartes soldier on through injuries that would leave a Guardsman bleeding out; it is described across Black Library fiction from minor cuts up to serious battlefield trauma.\n\nDesign: Reflavoured Rapid Healing (B79, 5 points): the RAW effect (+5 to effective HT for recovery rolls) undersells \"seals in seconds,\" so the design also folds in automatic stabilization against ongoing blood loss for the first turn after a wound, at no extra point cost — it's the same underlying \"clots fast\" phenomenon at two timescales.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Imperium",
						"Adeptus Astartes"
					],
					"base_points": 5
				},
				{
					"id": "tX0Nr6ZwLE9yYZ70G",
					"name": "Catalepsean Node",
					"reference": "B65",
					"local_notes": "Needs about 4 hours of sleep. On campaign the GM may let a Marine skip sleep entirely for days or weeks with no fatigue penalty (the hemispheres rest in turn); this is the fictional \"no sleep for weeks\" and is not bought as Doesn't Sleep.\n\nLore: A brainstem structure that lets the two cerebral hemispheres rest in alternation, so an Astartes only needs a few hours of true sleep where a human needs eight, and can go without any for days at a stretch on campaign. Distinct from the Sus-an Membrane, which is a full metabolic shutdown rather than efficient rest.\n\nDesign: Less Sleep 4 (B65, 2 points/level, the maximum of 4 levels): reduces sleep need from 8 hours to 4. 4 x 2 = 8 points. Doesn't Sleep (B50, 20 points) would overshoot: a Marine does eventually rest, and the weeks-awake feat is a campaign-length allowance, not a standing trait.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Imperium",
						"Adeptus Astartes"
					],
					"base_points": 8
				},
				{
					"id": "t6kL8OLDptyNbo9sT",
					"name": "Preomnor",
					"reference": "B81",
					"local_notes": "+8 to HT rolls to resist ingested poison and spoiled food. Not Immunity: weaponised or exotic toxins can still poison a Marine.\n\nLore: A supplementary \"pre-stomach\" that chemically breaks down and neutralizes toxins and spoiled matter in food before it reaches the true stomach, letting Astartes eat things — rotten rations, raw feral-world game, toxic fungus — that would sicken or kill an unaugmented human.\n\nDesign: Resistant (B81), Occasional: Ingested Poison, +8 to resist — base 10, x1/2 for the +8 tier = 5 points. Taken as a bonus rather than Immunity because the fiction has Marines poisoned by potent or engineered agents. Deliberately narrower than Oolitic Kidney below: this organ only ever sees toxins that arrive through the gut.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Imperium",
						"Adeptus Astartes"
					],
					"base_points": 5
				},
				{
					"id": "tA86NClD_SAjwmCXk",
					"name": "Omophagea",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Lets an Astartes extract genetic and biochemical information by consuming a portion of a creature's flesh or blood, surfacing it as hazy instinctive knowledge — described in the fiction as ritual consumption of a slain xenos to \"know\" something of it, rather than a controllable database query.\n\nDesign: No reliable, repeatable mechanical payoff to hang a point cost on — the fiction treats it as evocative, not a reliable Analyze/Detect power. Kept as a 1-point Perk (B21); a GM can hand out a one-off Hidden Lore or skill bonus after an appropriate scene at their discretion, with no fixed rule for it here.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Imperium",
						"Adeptus Astartes",
						"Perk"
					],
					"base_points": 1
				},
				{
					"id": "TrEtkRhj2nBM1BhYk",
					"name": "Multi-lung",
					"local_notes": "Lore: A supplementary lung that scrubs smoke, gas, and thin or tainted atmospheres, and banks extra oxygen for holding the breath through vacuum exposure, drowning, or a gas attack.\n\nDesign: Filter Lungs (B55, 5 points) for the \"breathe filthy air safely\" half; Breath-Holding 3 (B41, 2/level, 6 points) for the \"hold it a long time\" half. Container sums to 11 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Imperium",
						"Adeptus Astartes"
					],
					"container_type": "meta_trait",
					"children": [
						{
							"id": "td2UgmWr1TbD7JfIs",
							"name": "Filter Lungs",
							"reference": "B55",
							"base_points": 5
						},
						{
							"id": "tj0dIRuf1i3qBfW1j",
							"name": "Breath-Holding",
							"reference": "B41",
							"points_per_level": 2,
							"can_level": true,
							"levels": 3
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "TtYG_ZWLKvY4-GJAj",
					"name": "Occulobe",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Rewires the optic nerve and visual cortex for much sharper acuity and low-light performance, and hardens the eye against flash and glare — Astartes are consistently shown spotting targets and reading terrain at ranges no unaugmented eye could manage, and shrugging off blinding light that would stagger a human.\n\nDesign: Acute Vision 2 (B35, 2/level, 4 points) for the raw acuity; Night Vision 5 (B71, 1/level, 5 points) for the low-light performance; Protected Sense (Vision) (B78, 5 points) so flash/glare can't blind the organ outright. 14 points total.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Imperium",
						"Adeptus Astartes"
					],
					"container_type": "meta_trait",
					"children": [
						{
							"id": "tR-8HGXPFM5ER4pMD",
							"name": "Acute Vision",
							"reference": "B35",
							"points_per_level": 2,
							"can_level": true,
							"levels": 2
						},
						{
							"id": "tYGp9tHQZegLktn9h",
							"name": "Night Vision",
							"reference": "B71",
							"points_per_level": 1,
							"can_level": true,
							"levels": 5
						},
						{
							"id": "tpX4-j1oJmkZeTaG6",
							"name": "Protected Sense (Vision)",
							"reference": "B78",
							"base_points": 5
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "Tm_nx2v5aQehfv-4p",
					"name": "Lyman's Ear",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Reinforces the inner ear against the constant concussion of bolter fire and explosions while sharpening hearing and balance, so an Astartes can still track sound and stay upright through the kind of noise that would deafen and disorient an unaugmented soldier.\n\nDesign: Acute Hearing 2 (B35, 2/level, 4 points) plus Protected Sense (Hearing) (B78, 5 points) against deafening/concussive noise. 9 points total.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Imperium",
						"Adeptus Astartes"
					],
					"container_type": "meta_trait",
					"children": [
						{
							"id": "tNqyIvYpywfzDPMA4",
							"name": "Acute Hearing",
							"reference": "B35",
							"points_per_level": 2,
							"can_level": true,
							"levels": 2
						},
						{
							"id": "tbQ-LM2Kj0gKbCGPl",
							"name": "Protected Sense (Hearing)",
							"reference": "B78",
							"base_points": 5
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "tutNAxKP7jNPrkF3W",
					"name": "Sus-an Membrane",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Lets an Astartes drop, on command, into a deep hibernation that slows metabolism to near nothing — used for long void crossings in a survival capsule, or to ride out wounds that would otherwise be fatal by shutting down everything but core function. Depicted as something that takes real time to enter and leave, not an instant reflex.\n\nDesign: Custom build shown for transparency rather than a straight RAW pull: Doesn't Eat or Drink (B50, 10) + Doesn't Breathe (B49, 20) = 30 points of effect, but only while deliberately entering the trance, which takes about a minute either way — an Accessibility-style limitation worth roughly -70% (comparable to \"Trance Only\" in scope and severity). 30 x 0.3 = 9 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Imperium",
						"Adeptus Astartes"
					],
					"base_points": 9
				},
				{
					"id": "tJ0yp_SJCsNh9v9Mk",
					"name": "Melanchromic Organ",
					"reference": "B79",
					"local_notes": "Radiation Tolerance (PF 5) plus a 1-point Perk for voluntary pigment control.\n\nLore: Controls skin pigmentation and shields the body against radiation and hard UV, letting Astartes operate on irradiated battlefields and hostile worlds. Its baseline output varies by Chapter gene-seed — most notably the Salamanders, whose Melanchromic Organ runs permanently at full output (see the Chapter lens below).\n\nDesign: Radiation Tolerance (B79), PF 5 (10 points) for the shielding effect, plus a 1-point Perk for voluntary control over pigmentation (camouflage/recognition flavor, no fixed numeric benefit). 11 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Imperium",
						"Adeptus Astartes"
					],
					"base_points": 11
				},
				{
					"id": "tCp7uk_xBHJJ-sybE",
					"name": "Oolitic Kidney",
					"reference": "B81",
					"local_notes": "+8 to HT rolls to resist poison from any route. Not Immunity: exotic and weaponised agents (assassin toxins, Life-Eater, plague vectors) can still kill a Marine.\n\nLore: A backup kidney that aggressively filters toxins circulating in the blood — venoms, industrial poisons, battlefield chemical agents — rather than the ones Preomnor already caught at the gut.\n\nDesign: Resistant (B81), Common: Poison, +8 to resist — base 15, x1/2 for the +8 tier = 7.5, rounded down (Resistant rounds down) to 7 points. Priced above Preomnor because it covers poison from any route of entry, not just food. A bonus rather than Immunity because the fiction repeatedly has Marines poisoned by potent agents.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Imperium",
						"Adeptus Astartes"
					],
					"base_points": 7
				},
				{
					"id": "TgR3JBtG0ByN5wHaq",
					"name": "Neuroglottis",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Pushes taste and smell to a level that lets an Astartes identify an individual, a poison, or a chemical trace by scent alone, and track a quarry across terrain a hound couldn't follow.\n\nDesign: Discriminatory Smell (B49, 15 points, identify/track individuals and substances by scent) plus Acute Taste & Smell 3 (B35, 2/level, 6 points) for raw sensitivity. 21 points total.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Imperium",
						"Adeptus Astartes"
					],
					"container_type": "meta_trait",
					"children": [
						{
							"id": "t5c1ZmXaZqcmVOYeW",
							"name": "Discriminatory Smell",
							"reference": "B49",
							"base_points": 15
						},
						{
							"id": "tTpIzqiLIe5FgTz3C",
							"name": "Acute Taste & Smell",
							"reference": "B35",
							"points_per_level": 2,
							"can_level": true,
							"levels": 3
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "TL1PJt4Jor_gqQne1",
					"name": "Mucranoid",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Secretes a waxy, oily film that can be triggered to seal pores and orifices against vacuum, toxic atmosphere, and radiation, and that also insulates against extreme heat and cold.\n\nDesign: Sealed (B82, 15 points) covers vacuum/toxin/radiation sealing; Temperature Tolerance 5 (B93, 1/level, 5 points) covers the thermal insulation. 20 points total.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Imperium",
						"Adeptus Astartes"
					],
					"container_type": "meta_trait",
					"children": [
						{
							"id": "tgh9zWEpAHPAYU28U",
							"name": "Sealed",
							"reference": "B82",
							"base_points": 15
						},
						{
							"id": "tvcZPMisbsCXhU6x7",
							"name": "Temperature Tolerance",
							"reference": "B93",
							"points_per_level": 1,
							"can_level": true,
							"levels": 5
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "T3lkerB1XLtkd9QoI",
					"name": "Betcher's Gland",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Produces a corrosive, mildly toxic saliva. Fiction plays this as a minor, opportunistic weapon and a way to shrug off ingested poisons and diseased food in the mouth — not a primary attack for a Marine who has a bolter.\n\nDesign: Innate Attack (Corrosion) at a token 1d, range 1/3 yards (B61, roughly 3 points after the range restriction) for the spit, rolled against Innate Attack (Projectile) since spitting is a ranged act; 1-point Perk for the minor oral antitoxin effect (overlaps in concept with Preomnor, so kept nominal). 4 points total.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Imperium",
						"Adeptus Astartes"
					],
					"container_type": "meta_trait",
					"children": [
						{
							"id": "tNNtO2s8UbzQkig5_",
							"name": "Corrosive Spit",
							"base_points": 3,
							"weapons": [
								{
									"id": "WVDck9HNdis0iZy8n",
									"sv": 1,
									"damage": {
										"type": "cor",
										"base": "1d"
									},
									"accuracy": "1",
									"range": "1/3",
									"rate_of_fire": "1",
									"usage": "Spit",
									"defaults": [
										{
											"type": "skill",
											"name": {
												"compare": "is",
												"qualifier": "Innate Attack"
											},
											"specialization": {
												"compare": "is",
												"qualifier": "Projectile"
											}
										},
										{
											"type": "dx",
											"modifier": -4
										}
									]
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"id": "tpk2pxNnA54kmaWS6",
							"name": "Oral Poison Filter",
							"base_points": 1
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "tb76jN2PundPwnEEG",
					"name": "Progenoid Glands",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Two glands that mature over years into a bank of \"zygotes\" — genetic material an Apothecary harvests from the fallen to seed new recruits. Central to how a Chapter perpetuates and safeguards its gene-seed line, but they confer no combat benefit on the Marine who carries them; their value is entirely to the Chapter after death.\n\nDesign: 1-point Perk (B21): a narrative/plot-hook organ (its condition can matter for Apothecary rolls or a Chapter's gene-seed politics) with no combat mechanic of its own.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Imperium",
						"Adeptus Astartes",
						"Perk"
					],
					"base_points": 1
				},
				{
					"id": "tdTxT2agRS8fWKLT4",
					"name": "Black Carapace",
					"local_notes": "Lore: A synthetic interface grafted under the skin across the torso and spine and wired into the nervous system, grown last, only after a Scout has proven himself and is elevated to full Battle-Brother. It lets a suit of power armour read a Marine's nervous impulses directly, so the armour moves as an extension of the body rather than a piloted shell.\n\nDesign: The mechanical payoff (full reflexes, no bulk/encumbrance penalty, no clumsy manual controls) is a property of Astartes power armour equipment and belongs on that equipment's entry, not duplicated here, since a Marine without a suit to plug into gets nothing from it in play. Kept as a 1-point Perk marking that the interface exists and is a hard prerequisite for wearing power armour as intended.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Imperium",
						"Adeptus Astartes",
						"Perk"
					],
					"base_points": 1
				},
				{
					"id": "TK7mFJImqyl3RuHpe",
					"name": "Hypno-Indoctrination (Broken Oaths)",
					"local_notes": "Lore: The psycho-conditioning of the Astartes survives the Fall: a traitor still does not break under fire, still fights past the point where a baseline soldier would rout. What goes is the oath. Black Library's Horus Heresy and Chaos fiction show Legionaries who kept every reflex and every drilled habit and threw away Emperor, Chapter and Codex.\n\nDesign: The Astartes package's own Hypno-Indoctrination / Psycho-Conditioning (data/imperium/astartes/gene-seed.yaml) with its three oath disadvantages removed, as the Heretic Astartes lens directs: Combat Reflexes 15 + Fearlessness 4 (2/level) 8 + High Pain Threshold 10 + Single-Minded 5 = +38 in place of the package's net -2 (Duty -20, Sense of Duty -10, Code of Honor -10 left out). Everything else in the Astartes entry is included unchanged.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Chaos",
						"Heretic Astartes"
					],
					"container_type": "meta_trait",
					"children": [
						{
							"id": "tNp-QMwBAjU-YNjcg",
							"name": "Combat Reflexes",
							"reference": "B43",
							"base_points": 15
						},
						{
							"id": "tsYOSdENeyITSnsvW",
							"name": "Fearlessness",
							"reference": "B55",
							"points_per_level": 2,
							"can_level": true,
							"levels": 4
						},
						{
							"id": "t6REQyvbRV8bT1C2E",
							"name": "High Pain Threshold",
							"reference": "B59",
							"base_points": 10
						},
						{
							"id": "t4jwbP1fzPvMpjWdg",
							"name": "Single-Minded",
							"reference": "B85",
							"local_notes": "Relentless focus, now turned to the warband's ends.",
							"base_points": 5
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tjXxmrj98uIPVNLqL",
			"name": "Personal Advancement",
			"local_notes": "Lore: No two Battle-Brothers are physiologically identical even off the same gene-seed template, and what decades of live combat does to a body and mind that heal and learn far faster than baseline is depicted throughout Black Library fiction as making veterans noticeably sharper and tougher than newly-raised Battle-Brothers.\n\nDesign: DX+1 (20) + IQ+1 (20) + HT+1 (10) + Will+1 (5) + Per+1 (5) = 60 points of personal growth bought on top of the racial baseline.",
			"tags": [
