		{
			"id": "eKVp2A0YlA6W5dqvH",
			"description": "Frag Grenade",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The standard fragmentation grenade of the Departmento Munitorum, a fist-sized charge issued to virtually every Guardsman; a background constant across Black Library Guard fiction from Gaunt's Ghosts to the Ciaphas Cain novels.\n\nDesign: No framework.md anchor covers grenades, so this is built independently using GURPS's own explosive-damage convention — a concussion \"cr ex\" figure plus a bracketed fragmentation die, exactly the pattern data-format.md's own schema example uses. Concussion is set to a modest 3d cr ex (enough to injure at the centre, nowhere near a demolition charge) with a 4d cut fragmentation cloud (user direction, down from 6d: at 6d the fragments reached 30 yards and shredded massed infantry under B414) as the real threat to exposed infantry within a few yards. 4d cut (avg 14, no armour divisor) never penetrates flak (DR 30) or carapace (DR 70); only the Weak Points roll lets a fragment through flak. It is lethal to unarmoured troops in the open and useless against armour or fortifications.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"tech_level": "8",
			"legality_class": "2",
			"base_value": "20",
			"base_weight": "1 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "WecAKTZ0RNDn3BwVg",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "cr ex",
						"base": "3d",
						"fragmentation": "4d",
						"fragmentation_type": "cut"
					},
					"usage": "Thrown",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "dx",
							"modifier": -3
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Throwing"
							}
						}
					]
				}
			],
